group: D4h
formula: [PtCl4]^2-
construction: Fragment orbitals (extended Hückel)
headline: 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · not drawn: Cl4 internal: 8 levels, 16 e; tick Show all levels · labels in D<sub>4h</sub>\n3 levels match the calculation only loosely (overlap < 0.80)
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (Pt and Cl4). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the narrow column on the right. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, its energy in Hartree and the overlap value (1 is identical). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\n**Total electrons: 40** (Pt 8, Cl4 32).\n\nThe levels counted in the note under the diagram are model levels that sit almost entirely on the Cl4 and take no part in the interaction; they are counted, not drawn.\n\n**Caveats.** 3 levels match the calculation only loosely (overlap < 0.80). Extended Hückel puts empty antibonding orbitals tens of eV up, so an empty level more than 30 eV above the HOMO is drawn at the top of the axis with its model energy written beside it, or not at all when it sits almost entirely on one fragment. A loose match means no calculated orbital resembles the model level closely; read its calculated energy with care.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D4h; the code reported none.
verdict: differs The model puts 2B2g below 5B1g, the model puts 4Eu below 5B1g, the model puts 3A2u below 1Eg; your calculation has those the other way round (6 of 78 pairs of the 13 valence orbitals (overlap 0.56–0.97)).
